# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# playwright mcp session artifacts
/.playwright-mcp/

# scraped page cache + checkpoints for the evidence audit (regenerable, ~GBs)
/data/

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# graphify knowledge-graph output — a one-off discovery aid, regenerable, not a tracked artefact
graphify-out/

# pytest
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# agent worktrees — Claude Code drops isolated worktrees here, each a full second
# copy of the tree. Untracked they show as one noisy `??` entry; worse, vitest's
# include reaches `.claude/**`, so a live worktree doubles the collected suite
# (2082 tests became 4158) on a memory-capped machine. Also excluded in
# vitest.config.ts — both are needed, they solve different halves.
.claude/worktrees/

# the one sanctioned in-repo scratch directory (mantahostels#2089; docs/environment.md §12,
# which owns the rule and lists all four exclusions). Ignored here so scratch
# never reaches a commit, which also drops it from Biome's scope via biome.json's
# `vcs.useIgnoreFile` — deliberate, so the post-write core (scripts/lib/post-write.js) stops reformatting
# scratch on every write. biome.json and vitest.config.ts exclude it too, and
# neither reads this file, so all three are needed.
.claude/tmp/
# Machine-local state lives under .claude/tmp/markers/ (#2, F8). Some of it is
# NOT regenerable — the self-throttling and seat-utilisation histories and
# .pick-next/warm-fraction.jsonl — so never clear that directory wholesale.

# The history-trim watch file's throttle stamp (mantahostels#2617) — one reading a day,
# like the seat-utilisation stamp. The watch file itself,
# docs/data/history-trim-watch.jsonl, is TRACKED — unlike the machine-local
# histories, it must survive a fresh clone.
docs/data/history-trim-watch.jsonl.stamp

# precommit-gate-harness.test.ts's writeCheckerDelegates fixture — written into
# the real scripts/ (the delegate re-execs an absolute ROOT path, so a
# throwaway repo's own scripts/ can't stand in) and removed per test; ignored
# so a run killed between the write and its afterEach doesn't strand an
# untracked file under Biome's scope (mantahostels#2073).
/scripts/__precommit-gate-harness-test-fixture-*.js

# Claude Code's own type declarations, which a mod type-checks against:
# proprietary, with no grant to redistribute them (#1960).
# scripts/typecheck-mods.js copies them in from the plugin-authoring skill.
.claude/skills/*/.claude-plugin/types/

# Discovery-interview entries — Data Pribadi under processing-register.md R14,
# and erasable only outside git: a tracked entry survives deletion in history,
# in every clone, and with GitHub, Inc., an independent controller of this
# repository's content on a free personal account (mantahostels#1564, mantahostels#1569). The tracked
# docs/discovery-log.md keeps the schema and the aggregate counters only.
/private/
